Phase OS-13: Kernel IPC & Synchronization Subsystem - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/ipc_msgq.asm (Message Queue IPC)
   - Base ID: 901
   - System V-style message queues for inter-process communication
   - Features: queue creation/destruction, message send/receive with priority, blocking/non-blocking modes, queue limits (max messages, max bytes), message types, queue statistics, permission checking
   - Data structures: msg_queue_t (id, key, msg_count, byte_count, max_msgs, max_bytes, permissions, owner, first_msg, last_msg, active), msg_t (type, priority, size, data[256], next)
   - API: ipc_msgq_init, ipc_msgq_create, ipc_msgq_destroy, ipc_msgq_send, ipc_msgq_receive, ipc_msgq_peek, ipc_msgq_stat
   - Capacity: 32 queues, 256 messages per queue, 256 bytes per message
   - Pattern: follow kernel/net_tcp.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/ipc_sem.asm (Semaphore Synchronization)
   - Base ID: 902
   - Counting semaphores for process synchronization
   - Features: semaphore creation/destruction, P (wait/decrement) operation, V (signal/increment) operation, trywait (non-blocking), timedwait with timeout, semaphore value query, ownership tracking
   - Data structures: sem_t (id, key, value, max_value, wait_queue[16], wait_count, owner, permissions, active)
   - API: ipc_sem_init, ipc_sem_create, ipc_sem_destroy, ipc_sem_wait, ipc_sem_trywait, ipc_sem_timedwait, ipc_sem_post, ipc_sem_getvalue
   - Capacity: 64 semaphores, 16 waiters per semaphore
   - Pattern: follow kernel/net_tcp.asm style

3. kernel/ipc_shm.asm (Shared Memory IPC)
   - Base ID: 903
   - Shared memory segments for high-performance IPC
   - Features: segment creation/destruction, attach/detach operations, permission control, segment size management, reference counting, segment statistics, lock/unlock for atomic operations
   - Data structures: shm_seg_t (id, key, size, addr, attach_count, ref_count, permissions, owner, locked, active), shm_attach_t (pid, addr, seg_id, active)
   - API: ipc_shm_init, ipc_shm_create, ipc_shm_destroy, ipc_shm_attach, ipc_shm_detach, ipc_shm_lock, ipc_shm_unlock, ipc_shm_stat
   - Capacity: 16 segments, 64KB each, 32 attachments per segment
   - Pattern: follow kernel/net_tcp.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

